<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Zanzibar War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1896</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Zanzibar War was a brief conflict on 27 August 1896 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the Sultanate of Zanzibar. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamad-bin-thuwaini">Hamad bin Thuwaini</a> died, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-bin-barghash">Khalid bin Barghash</a> seized the palace without British approval and refused an ultimatum to stand down. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> warships bombarded the palace, and the fighting ended in under an hour, often called the shortest war in recorded history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-zanzibar-war.jpg" alt="Anglo-Zanzibar War" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Mohun · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AngloZanzibarWar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
